    "q-102322": {
      "dom_id": "step-q102322",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Given the **orthonormal** basis $B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\}$ of ${R}^{2},$ find $[x]_{B}$ if $x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthonormal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=x\\cdot {q}_{i}.$ Computing the components of $x,$ we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]=\\sqrt{3}-1 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\end{aligned}]=1+\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}-1 \\\\ 1+\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-102322-a",
